  "goodToKnow": "Säkular means secular, not religious: ein säkularer Staat, die säkulare Gesellschaft. The native synonym is weltlich. Germany separates church and state but cooperates with churches: the state collects Kirchensteuer for them. In 2022, for the first time, fewer than half of Germans belonged to the two major churches. Die Säkularisation of 1803 transferred church lands to secular rulers. In older German, säkular also meant once a century."
